    "segments": [
      {
        "role": "leader",
        "speaker": "Leader",
        "sourceStart": 8,
        "sourceEnd": 241,
        "text": "Before Saturday's visit, I want to explain our dune-monitoring plan. We are not planting anything this month. We are taking photographs and recording where people leave the boardwalk. That will help us choose places for future signs.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "e394cfd0f991e4fbe37ed28b191344993d04c4f243f322805c243e6f86087796",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0
      },
      {
        "role": "volunteer",
        "speaker": "Volunteer",
        "sourceStart": 253,
        "sourceEnd": 310,
        "text": "Last year we counted footprints. Are we doing that again?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "6a54f051dccb04e3fb41917dc212752bc312d4aae597e3bcefeb68fc6224e649",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leader",
        "speaker": "Leader",
        "sourceStart": 319,
        "sourceEnd": 623,
        "text": "No. Footprints can remain for several days, so one busy afternoon can affect several counts. This time we will observe actual movements during fixed periods. Each pair will watch one access point for twenty minutes, followed by a ten-minute break. We will use the same periods at all three access points.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "930524a06936fb52dff112bd562032a192059cb2c8f1f61f5d325e7235c01ef0",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "volunteer",
        "speaker": "Volunteer",
        "sourceStart": 635,
        "sourceEnd": 677,
        "text": "Should we tell people to stay on the path?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "3652f4ba41030cbf547c9b134e023fee820ca739329a16f0133986edb0d0d3d7",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leader",
        "speaker": "Leader",
        "sourceStart": 686,
        "sourceEnd": 940,
        "text": "A ranger will deal with safety. Your job is to observe without starting conversations about the research. If we remind people while counting, their behaviour may change because we are there. Of course, tell the ranger immediately if someone is in danger.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "64bb1a2c06500e2750731f77feb5015097e7e7ae1c0bf63ced97e2b506af7f52",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "volunteer",
        "speaker": "Volunteer",
        "sourceStart": 952,
        "sourceEnd": 985,
        "text": "Where should we take photographs?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "9a010ddb3b029ad4c0d9254ed475f69392d52a3551242d90e5580f11f8730aa3",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leader",
        "speaker": "Leader",
        "sourceStart": 994,
        "sourceEnd": 1281,
        "text": "Use the painted post as your starting point. Hold the camera at chest height and face north. The pictures are for comparing the visible area over time. They are not measurements of the amount of sand. Please avoid identifiable faces; wait a moment if someone is directly in front of you.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "2cb4f5c6a03dcc33dd2861650a99d6f4c94fc167696a61701efb29b3cf060a76",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "volunteer",
        "speaker": "Volunteer",
        "sourceStart": 1293,
        "sourceEnd": 1335,
        "text": "Do we enter the dune to get a better view?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "8c97e1675cf9c5fcdd27d4401a80bfc0707fc66c3ae0ec17b12ecbf4cbfe9c4b",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leader",
        "speaker": "Leader",
        "sourceStart": 1344,
        "sourceEnd": 1672,
        "text": "No. Stay on the boardwalk. The western access point is closed because a section is damaged, so we will replace it with the central one. The weather forecast is dry, but if the wind becomes strong enough to blow loose sand into our equipment, we will stop and note the time. We will not record a stopped session as zero visitors.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "aad9edfbb1333f8c4e876c557cfa60c053b5e5b2bd59f4be0efdf982999519a9",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "volunteer",
        "speaker": "Volunteer",
        "sourceStart": 1684,
        "sourceEnd": 1711,
        "text": "When do you need the forms?",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-GuyNeural",
        "textHash": "517fcf8d99d349139c90a15bd49c33d96935a0ef0c98da6e902b8e3d96185c1a",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      },
      {
        "role": "leader",
        "speaker": "Leader",
        "sourceStart": 1720,
        "sourceEnd": 1899,
        "text": "Upload them by Sunday evening, including any difficulties. A form with a clear note about missing observations is more useful than a form that looks complete but contains guesses.",
        "boundary": "turn",
        "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural",
        "textHash": "68c0692f916afb928de07cb03d97b6bb0e275b592fa75bdd26fce93d9bdbed62",
        "pauseBeforeSeconds": 0.45
      }
    ]
  },
